menu "Orb display experiments"
    config ORB_DISPLAY_LIVE_DOUBLE_BUFFER
        bool "Overlap live bands when no visible scene reads its backdrop"
        default y
        depends on ORB_DISPLAY_INTERNAL_DOUBLE_BUFFER
        help
            Inspect the active screen and system layers before each refresh.
            If no visible object has a backdrop blur, the existing internal
            arena may use two half-bands even for large damage. Any live blur
            keeps the guarded full band. No extra DMA arena or PSRAM drawing.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_SCROLL_TRACE
        bool "Capture input, scroll, refresh and UI scheduling timestamps"
        default n
        depends on ORB_DEVTOOLS && SPIRAM
        help
            Lead-only attribution capture started by bench_scroll. Retain up to
            2048 timestamped events in PSRAM, plus complete-frame interval
            histograms and wait totals that continue after overflow. No console
            output or per-frame allocation during capture. Packed CRC chunks are
            emitted after capture. Disable for final throughput gates.

    config ORB_RENDER_FUSED_GLASS
        bool "Fuse reduced glass reconstruction, tint, coverage and rim"
        default n
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            Experimental internal-SRAM glass kernel with an area-averaged
            reduced backdrop and screen-anchored RGB565 dithering. Reuse the
            shared antialiased SDF masks and IMU light. Unsupported formats,
            incomplete backdrop support and failed admission use the reference
            renderer. Keep the existing 84-row internal band and transfer path.
            Measure both visual differences and whole-frame board performance.

    config ORB_RENDER_ROWS_AT_SIZE
        bool "Draw moving matte rows from native-size glyph atlases"
        default y
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            Sixteen-size glyph coverage atlas (on by default since the 2026-10-27
            board A/B: scroll 18.4 -> 21.5 fps, draw 40.5 -> 32.7 ms) for supported
            curved-list rows. Blend glyphs directly into the internal output
            band instead of transforming full row rasters. Keep native static
            rows cached and unsupported content on the reference raster path.
            Font, style and accessibility changes retire the admitted atlas.
            Native-size quantization requires independent visual review.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_TE_PACING
        bool "TE deadline scheduling with measured motion admission"
        default n
        help
            Coalesce refreshes before layout/raster work without blocking input
            timers. Use the measured awake-panel TE grid and preserve per-band
            scan avoidance. Skip expired slots; count actual final SPI deadline
            hits and misses. Both scrolling and games may use every TE. Slow
            content uses a measured integer divisor, reevaluated after eight
            initial warm frames, then over 16-frame blocks. One isolated work
            outlier stays a reported miss instead of lowering the whole rate.
            No idle TE redraws, new DMA storage, or panel clock changes.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_RETAINED_SETTLED_ONLY
        bool "Suspend retained material preparation during backdrop motion"
        default n
        depends on ORB_DISPLAY_RETAINED_MATERIAL
        help
            Use the exact compatibility blur while scrolling/parallax changes
            content. Re-admit retained maps after 120 ms of settled content.
            Avoid rebuilding retained source/maps/bases on every moving frame.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_GLASS_SOLID_FAST
        bool "Skip blur kernels for exactly uniform RGB565 backdrops"
        default y
        help
            Inspect the complete sampled control rectangle within its band,
            excluding stride padding, using exact bulk comparisons. Uniform black or
            solid input uses the identical tint/AA/screen-dither reconstruction
            without filtering or allocating filter/map scratch. Nonuniform content
            retains the reference live blur, even for a single changed pixel.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_GLASS_SPARSE_MASKS
        bool "Draw exact SDF masks using their nonzero row spans"
        default n
        help
            Retain bounded per-row spans with shared glass masks and skip fully
            transparent padding/interiors in A8 image draws. Keep exact original
            coverage and blend functions. Independent board A/B experiment.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_RENDER_ACCOUNTING
        bool "Stage 0: account whole updates, preparation and presentation cadence"
        default n
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            Bounded counters around refresh preparation and final SPI result
            drain, 1 ms completion interval buckets and the last eight band
            draw/queue/DMA timestamps. No hot-loop output or per-frame allocation.
            Keep normal frame/DRAW/WAIT/HOLD/WIRE diagnostics unchanged.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_RETAINED_MATERIAL
        bool "Stage 1: retain exact settled glass maps and material bases"
        default n
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            Retain exact untinted maps and RGB565 bases for managed Orb glass.
            Dependency revisions include lower content transforms/opacity/clips,
            z-order, source content, theme and accessibility. Geometry, tint,
            destination dither and format key the final base separately. Light
            changes restore the base without traversing unchanged source rows.
            Unsupported drawing, allocation failure or incomplete dependencies
            use the exact compatibility renderer. No band/transport changes.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_GLASS_SINGLE_PASS
        bool "Cull off-band glass tasks before dispatch"
        default n
        help
            Avoid blur dispatch for controls outside a band's clip. The existing
            whole-control band guard retains complete control samples. Does not
            reuse pixels by object identity or read unwritten later bands.
            Current 84-row guards already execute about three real blurs per
            scroll frame; extra profiler calls mostly return without work.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_GLASS_MOTION_QUALITY
        bool "Use averaged quarter-resolution glass during scrolling"
        default n
        help
            Experimental motion-only backdrop downsampling. Retains full-size
            antialiased edges, bilinear reconstruction and screen Bayer dither;
            restores the normal quality after scrolling settles. Requires visual
            review on the panel; host timing does not establish device FPS.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_RASTER_SCALE_CACHE
        bool "Cache exact scaled opaque RGB565 row variants in PSRAM"
        default n
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            Bounded LRU of exact integer-scale variants, built before DRAW.
            Image tasks reuse scaled color and coverage as plain IMAGE blits;
            source content, geometry and format changes invalidate the variants.
            Opacity remains exact. No scale quantization or extra internal DMA
            arena. Measure whole-frame time as well as DRAW and build counters.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_RGB565_SCALE_FAST
        bool "Specialize exact scale-only opaque RGB565 transforms"
        default n
        help
            Hoist constant row coordinates/weights and increment integer X
            coordinates in the opaque scale-only filter. Generic transforms
            retain their existing checked AA edges and fallback. No retained
            lookup storage, no additional DMA buffer, no coarse scale steps.
            Independent of the variant cache; also accelerates cold variants.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_RASTER_COVER_CHECK
        bool "Require opaque native-scale cached roots for cover skipping"
        default y
        help
            Correctness fix: a cached child cannot cover its parent's faded or
            scaled composite. Prevents stale pixels when rows move near the
            bezel. Disable only to reproduce the old partial-redraw defect.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_RASTER_SCALE_CACHE_KIB
        int "PSRAM budget for exact scaled row variants (KiB)"
        default 512
        range 64 1024
        depends on ORB_DISPLAY_RASTER_SCALE_CACHE
        help
            Includes retained variant pixels and metadata. Source raster bytes
            and temporary construction memory are reported separately. Current
            frame variants are pinned; misses fall back safely when all fit
            candidates cannot be admitted within this budget.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_DRAW_PROFILE
        bool "Collect bounded software draw-task benchmark timings"
        default n
        depends on ORB_DEVTOOLS && SPIRAM
        help
            Lead-only attribution build. Two timestamps and native atomic
            counters per software draw task, grouped by type/widget class and
            transformed image path. Benchmark emits phase deltas only after
            returning to the original screen. Separate hotspot stages show
            rows preparation/draw and glass preparation/downsample/filter/compose.
            DRAW_EVENTS also includes synchronous custom painting and task drains.
            Preparation can precede DRAW; GLASS_PREPARE includes its children.
            About 1.4 KiB static counters and 26 KiB PSRAM snapshots; no profiler
            serial flood while drawing.
            Wall time includes preemption and concurrent workers overlap, so
            summed task time can exceed display DRAW. Disable for final FPS.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_TALL_BANDS
        bool "Render in 104-row bands instead of 84"
        default n
        help
            Spend another 18,640 internal DMA bytes per draw buffer to reduce
            band boundaries. Keeps the glass guard and TE scheduling intact.
            Measure with networking, reconnect and OTA before accepting: this
            also makes the optional second buffer harder to admit.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_INTERNAL_DOUBLE_BUFFER
        bool "Split the render arena for small refreshes and cached navigation"
        default y
        depends on !ORB_DISPLAY_PSRAM_PIPELINE
        help
            Reserve two aligned half-bands in the original early draw arena
            (48 extra bytes at 84 rows). After accepted hello, require 24 KiB
            internal/DMA free and an 8 KiB largest DMA block. Use both halves
            for complete small live invalidations or an explicitly certified
            immutable full-screen navigation compositor with no live blur.
            Other redraws use the full band so glass blur is never sliced.
            Navigation bypasses the live glass band guard only while certified;
            its snapshots already contain the settled controls. Fence DMA before
            each switch and before returning from snapshots to live content.
            Admission is a snapshot, not a guarantee of future audio/OTA fit.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_INTERNAL_IMAGE_SCRATCH
        bool "Prefer internal RAM for software image transform scratch"
        default n
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            Route transient image transform tiles through the bounded draw-only
            allocator. Leave general LVGL objects and raster caches unchanged.
            All draw scratch shares a 16 KiB internal cap with reserve checks;
            rejected allocations fall back to PSRAM. Measure before enabling.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_INTERNAL_BLUR_SCRATCH
        bool "Prefer internal RAM for software blur scratch"
        default n
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            Route transient blur arrays/LUTs through the same bounded allocator.
            Leave persistent backdrop-cache payload in PSRAM. Independent from
            image scratch so the lead can isolate their effects.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_INTERNAL_DRAW_MASKS
        bool "Prefer internal RAM for software draw scanline masks"
        default n
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            Route transient software primitive masks through the same bounded
            draw-only allocator. Disabled kinds use explicit PSRAM even for
            small masks; enable only after measuring the internal preference.

    config ORB_DISPLAY_PSRAM_PIPELINE
        bool "Copy display bands to two PSRAM DMA snapshots"
        default n
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3 && SPIRAM
        help
            Keep LVGL's single internal DMA draw buffer, and copy each completed
            band to one of two fixed PSRAM snapshots. This overlaps drawing with
            panel transfer, at the cost of PSRAM bandwidth and about 154 KiB of
            PSRAM. Direct PSRAM DMA underflow disables the pipeline until reboot
            and requests a full redraw using the blocking internal buffer.
            Experimental: compare frame latency and transfer errors on hardware
            with Wi-Fi and the intended workload before enabling by default.
endmenu
